Same issue with Python projects. Files are being auto-formatted despite explicitly disabling formatters in `opencode.json`.

I've tried disabling `uv` and `ruff` both globally and per-project, but the formatting still occurs:
```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "formatter": {
    "uv": {
      "disabled": true
    },
    "ruff": {
      "disabled": true
    },
    "prettier": {
      "disabled": true
    }
  }
}
```

The configuration appears to be ignored completely.

@sai-sy we talked to openai this remains an issue for a lot of people because of how the responses api works. 

You can try getting around it by doing this:
```
 "openai": {
      "models": {
        "gpt-5": {
          "options": {
            "include": ["reasoning.encrypted_content"],
            "store": false,
          },
        },
      },
    },
```

Just do that for the openai models u use, we previously couldn't do this automaticaly because of some restrictions but I think they updated it for us actually

@kballand try this:
```
        "includeUsage": false,
```

So:
```
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "provider": {
    "databricks": {
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "name": "Databricks",
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "https://dbc-xxxxxxxx.cloud.databricks.com/serving-endpoints",
        "apiKey": "YOUR_API_KEY",
        "includeUsage": false, // <<< THIS RIGHT HERE
      },
      "models": {
        "databricks-claude-sonnet-4-5": {
          "name": "Databricks Claude Sonnet 4.5"
        }
      }
    }
